    {
      "id": "claim_66618fcf9a4a4207af947e6378ac0346",
      "statement": "Scrubbing is applied redundantly at every graph boundary rather than once centrally: individual nodes (preprocess, retrieve, evaluate, generate, safety, safety_finalize, history) scrub their own inputs/outputs before writing to graph state, and engine_record.build_result re-scrubs the final answer, raw_answer, follow_ups, and router telemetry (dropping sensitive-keyed telemetry fields via ROUTER_SENSITIVE_KEYS) before assembling the turn's result, which becomes checkpointed state.",
